{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere","id":1303671,"title":"Prototype00\u2019s Lunar Ess2 Charm picks with no Ess2 Pre-reqs (Glory Sphere)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-08T17:41:46-07:00","id":1303671,"title":"Prototype00\u2019s Lunar Ess2 Charm picks with no Ess2 Pre-reqs (Glory Sphere)","content":"Did you know that Lunars can pick one Ess2 Charm at character Creation from whatever Attribute they want? Caveats are:<br /> <br /> 1: You need the Glory Sphere Greater Dependent Hearthstone, either buy it with Merits or grow it with Radiant Basilisc Jewel (you also need another non-dependent Hearthstone to power it, just pick up a Stable one for 2 Merit dots)<br /> 2. The Ess2 Charm can have no Ess2 pre-reqs and you need all the Ess1 Pre-reqs<br /> 3. You need to meet the Attribute Minimum (TBH it\u2019s probably 5) for the Charm.<br /> <br /> Since Lunars are, I think, reasonably incentivised to go for this option as compared to other Exalted, I thought I\u2019d do a survey of the limited number of Ess2 charms available for this out there.<br /> <br /> Err... when I get home from work today!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-08-2019, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T08:16:59-07:00","id":1303781,"title":"","content":"<b>Dexterity</b><br /> <br /> Unerring Fang Technique (1m, Supplemental, Striking Mospid Method): Hmm, 1m for 1 extra success whenever you spend a full excellency and you can cheat and not stunt it and just spend 5 motes? Its a nice workhorse charm, not flashy, but not bad.<br /> <br /> <b>Intelligence</b><br /> <br /> Shadow Hand Invocation (2m, Reflexive, One Turn, Cloaked in Moonfire): As stated in another thread, you should be able to flurry Sorceries in combat as a Pestletail with Full Defense and the Natural Shield (OO) mutation (attach it to your Tell) until the cows come home and you are basically a brick wall.<br /> <br /> <b>Perception</b><br /> <br /> Instinctive Supremacy Approach (3i, Reflexive, Wolf-Eye Advantage): A full Free Excellency on the 1st round of every battle if you win Join Battle is bonkers good.<br /> <br /> <b>Stamina</b><br /> <br /> Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace (10m, 1wp, Simple, One Scene, Durant Quicksilver Adaptation): Probably a Lunar Martial Artist with Silken Robes best friend.<br /> <br /> Mamba and Cobra if you are doing poison shennanigans.<br /> <br /> Undying God Beast Perfection ( - , permannt, DBT, Halting the Scarlet Flow): Hmm, it doesn't say you need to do damage. Risky but you could heal all the way up just by spamming decisives every round, couldn't you? I need to give some more thought about making the offensive angle of this charm better...<br /> <br /> <b>Strength</b><br /> <br /> Claws of the Silver Moon (5m, 1wp, Simple, Ferocious Biting Tooth, Divine Predator Strike): Either for your Scary DBT form or for Hungry Hippo with 10 overwhelming bites, nothing comes close.<br /> <br /> Hmm, not too many, thank goodness (my criteria were quite strict it seems). Did I miss any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-09-2019, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T08:58:20-07:00","id":1303785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303781#post1303781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dexterity</b><br /> <br /> Unerring Fang Technique (1m, Supplemental, Striking Mospid Method): Hmm, 1m for 1 extra success whenever you spend a full excellency and you can cheat and not stunt it and just spend 5 motes? Its a nice workhorse charm, not flashy, but not bad.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And get an extra dice for each 10. I think it's pretty tech, as workhorse charms go. You can't use it on decisives though.<br /> <br /> Still, I have to confess that I wouldn't buy a background and use another charm just to be able to buy it. Whereas Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace seems much more powerful, for the right character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T09:48:12-07:00","id":1303792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, I have to confess that I wouldn't buy a background and use another charm just to be able to buy it. Whereas Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace seems much more powerful, for the right character. </div> </div> </div>Not sure what this means...?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T09:58:07-07:00","id":1303795,"title":"","content":"I mean that, while I think Unerring Fang Technique is good, I don't think it's worth anyone spending 6 dots of merits just to be allowed to buy it early.<br /> <br /> Whereas for a martial artist in silken armour, maybe Moonsilver Carapace is worth it. And for a hippo-Lunar, Claws of the Silver Moon is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T16:38:40-07:00","id":1303845,"title":"","content":"Just take Radiant Basilisc Jewel at Character Creation.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree that workhorse is probably not what you want at the investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-09-2019, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T23:50:10-07:00","id":1303895,"title":"","content":"You missed Mountainous Spirit Expression in Strength, for those who'd like to be huge; stiff upkeep but out of combat, hey, you've got a couple of hearthstones, in combat you're more able to passively tank stuff and rely on the offensive spend instead.<br /> <br /> As an added bonus that means the no upkeep upgrade is merely at E3!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T03:36:11-07:00","id":1303907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303895#post1303895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You missed Mountainous Spirit Expression in Strength, for those who'd like to be huge; stiff upkeep but out of combat, hey, you've got a couple of hearthstones, in combat you're more able to passively tank stuff and rely on the offensive spend instead.<br /> <br /> As an added bonus that means the no upkeep upgrade is merely at E3!</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the ability to already turn into a Legendary Sized critter at Ess1 dis-inclined me from choosing it. <br /> <br /> Though if you are a grappler DBT Falcon Stylist, nothing could be finer. Everything unopposed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-10-2019, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T04:12:53-07:00","id":1303911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303907#post1303907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose the ability to already turn into a Legendary Sized critter at Ess1 dis-inclined me from choosing it. <br /> <br /> Though if you are a grappler DBT Falcon Stylist, nothing could be finer. Everything unopposed!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but i don't want to be a critter, I want to be ME. Ir rather, my character. And yes, it certainly lets you &quot;grapple&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T06:42:42-07:00","id":1303929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303795#post1303795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that, while I think Unerring Fang Technique is good, I don't think it's worth anyone spending 6 dots of merits just to be allowed to buy it early.<br /> <br /> Whereas for a martial artist in silken armour, maybe Moonsilver Carapace is worth it. And for a hippo-Lunar, Claws of the Silver Moon is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually disagree with that. Moonsilver carpace and claws of the silver moon are absurdly expensive to just an artifact. You really aren't going to be using them that often unless you have an upgrade that removes the willpower use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T07:36:21-07:00","id":1303939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303929#post1303929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually disagree with that. Moonsilver carpace and claws of the silver moon are absurdly expensive to just an artifact. You really aren't going to be using them that often unless you have an upgrade that removes the willpower use.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want acquisition of Artifact weapon and armour from which one can't be divested or denied to have no Willpower cost?<br /> <br /> &quot;Just&quot; an Artifact seems like looking at them with an outlook of when they were just bigger weapon stats.<br /> <br /> Besides, there's always an option to effectively remove a Willpower cost by following up summoning one's Artifact by employing it in a sufficiently interesting and creative stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T07:42:26-07:00","id":1303940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303939#post1303939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You want acquisition of Artifact weapon and armour from which one can't be divested or denied to have no Willpower cost?<br /> <br /> &quot;Just&quot; an Artifact seems like looking at them with an outlook of when they were just bigger weapon stats.<br /> <br /> Besides, there's always an option to effectively remove a Willpower cost by following up summoning one's Artifact by employing it in a sufficiently interesting and creative stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Merit wise, the artifact and this hearthstone are roughly the same. While there are advantages to the charms the willpower requirement is a massive drawback. It's not something you can use every fight because that willpower adds up. Especially if you use both carapace and claws. And not every stunt is going to be good enough to do willpower. Not if you use them that often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:12:36-07:00","id":1303947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303940#post1303940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not something you can use every fight because that willpower adds up.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many fights is a character getting into per session?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And not every stunt is going to be good enough to do willpower. Not if you use them that often.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:16:55-07:00","id":1303949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303947#post1303947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many fights is a character getting into per session?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How often?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does depend on the game. I've had a few that are day by day with larger tracks of time off in between sessions. Which leads to situations where you have to carefully spend willpower because it doesn't come back quickly. Willpower isn't just used for powers. It's also used to resist mental defenses or when you really need to boost an action. It's also in a much more limited pool than motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:26:33-07:00","id":1303951,"title":"","content":"I often run out of willpower (not because I spend it like crazy, though Irresistable Questioning Technique did once eat up 4 of my wp points in one scene, but rather because that game tends to be 1-2 days a session and we don't get many 2-pt stunts), but 1wp for a scene-long buff doesn't seem expensive to me. It's cheaper than the many instant charms that cost 1wp. It's certainly much more worthwhile than boosting an action with 1 success.<br /> <br /> I mean, 1wp a fight is, for me, about 1 wp every 2-3 sessions. Because that's how often there's a (serious)* fight.<br /> <br /> *As opposed to, like &quot;you get into a fight with some mortal guards&quot;, which hardly requires Moonsilver Carapace.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-10-2019, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:40:51-07:00","id":1303955,"title":"","content":"On the others: I think Mamba-and-Cobra Mastery isn't utterly amazing, but for a poison-based combat strategy, it's a very appealing character gen pick. Otherwise all you've got is Adder-Fang, basically, which isn't really better than just having a set of poisoned knives. But Mamba-And-Cobra pushes it much further, as duration is also difficulty with poisons. And when you get to Essence 2, get a second purchase of Mamba-and-Cobra so that they always get poisoned for at least 1 round is very good (not to mention more options).<br /> <br /> Instinctive Supremacy Approach isn't a brilliant charm at Essence 5. I'd rather keep the 3i.<br /> But at Essence 1, when your mote pool is pretty damn small, then I think, if you've got a very good join battle pool, saving 8-10 motes is very good.<br /> On the other hand, 3i is equivalent to 6 motes on your Join Battle. So I'd say the free excellency is only worth it for people who are a)going to get a big Initiative, so they can use the charm, and b)can stunt to get a cap of 10 on their first attack (so Dex 5 and another attribute at 5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:45:12-07:00","id":1303956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303951#post1303951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often run out of willpower (not because I spend it like crazy, though Irresistable Questioning Technique did once eat up 4 of my wp points in one scene, but rather because that game tends to be 1-2 days a session and we don't get many 2-pt stunts), but 1wp for a scene-long buff doesn't seem expensive to me. It's cheaper than the many instant charms that cost 1wp. It's certainly much more worthwhile than boosting an action with 1 success.<br /> <br /> I mean, 1wp a fight is, for me, about 1 wp every 2-3 sessions. Because that's how often there's a (serious)* fight.<br /> <br /> *As opposed to, like &quot;you get into a fight with some mortal guards&quot;, which hardly requires Moonsilver Carapace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really just thinking of it's necessity long term to use that hearthstone with. I mean they're nice charms but they aren't exactly cheap in cost.<br /> <br /> Honestly, this stone seems a lot more useful for E3-5 charms maybe 6 since it technically doesn't stop E6 charms but a lot of the amazing charms don't come until later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-10-2019, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:57:28-07:00","id":1303959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303955#post1303955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instinctive Supremacy Approach isn't a brilliant charm at Essence 5. I'd rather keep the 3i.<br /> But at Essence 1, when your mote pool is pretty damn small, then I think, if you've got a very good join battle pool, saving 8-10 motes is very good.<br /> On the other hand, 3i is equivalent to 6 motes on your Join Battle. So I'd say the free excellency is only worth it for people who are a)going to get a big Initiative, so they can use the charm, and b)can stunt to get a cap of 10 on their first attack (so Dex 5 and another attribute at 5).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have Sense-Sharpening Change up the cost is waved and the charm only costs 4m.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T09:09:20-07:00","id":1303964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303955#post1303955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instinctive Supremacy Approach isn't a brilliant charm at Essence 5. I'd rather keep the 3i.<br /> But at Essence 1, when your mote pool is pretty damn small, then I think, if you've got a very good join battle pool, saving 8-10 motes is very good.<br /> On the other hand, 3i is equivalent to 6 motes on your Join Battle. So I'd say the free excellency is only worth it for people who are a)going to get a big Initiative, so they can use the charm, and b)can stunt to get a cap of 10 on their first attack (so Dex 5 and another attribute at 5).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to pair it with the Predator's Menace Latent ability and just crash everyone with a free full excellency to an Instill &quot;Fear Me&quot; threaten check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T19:27:56-07:00","id":1304074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1303929#post1303929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually disagree with that. Moonsilver carpace and claws of the silver moon are absurdly expensive to just an artifact. You really aren't going to be using them that often unless you have an upgrade that removes the willpower use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure that Socketing the Revolutionary Dog hearthstone (it\u2019s Stable!) probably is a good bet to offset Willpower costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:04:00-07:00","id":1304355,"title":"","content":"Shout out to Silver Lion Supremacy if you're a smart-guy tactician rather than a smart-guy sorcerer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Some more detail: Silver Lion Supremacy gives you those sweet non-charm dice on a Strategic manuever roll and it keys off Might, not Size. So even a small force of significantly empowered Followers will make a big difference. Assuming you describe your gambit, those babies are Successes.<br /> <br /> Combine with Raiton Follows After for its whopping 1m cost and you're getting extra non-charm dice from every 10 you roll, and the prereq Argent Pack Formation will basically end any penalties you might be concerned about.<br /> <br /> Another quick note, all of these key off the Might of any Allied battle group. Which means if there are NPC DBs on your side you don't even need the Followers merit.<br /> <br /> But you should have it, because this charm just turned you into Lunar Soren and you need some Laguz buddies.<br /> <br /> EDIT EDIT: Oh and if you're attacking a crashed opponent with RFA bc you're nasty like that you get basically a free full INT excellency as non-charm dice. Basically if you want to End someone's shit and you have even like, four magical friends, it's not out of the question that you could be rolling more Non-charm bonuses than your capped excellency is giving you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-11-2019, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:19:12-07:00","id":1304364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1304355#post1304355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shout out to Silver Lion Supremacy if you're a smart-guy tactician rather than a smart-guy sorcerer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Basically between that and Argent Pack formation, even a small force of magically reinforced Followers will absolutely destroy much larger and more qualified opponents in strategic manuevers.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I am going to be perfectly honest, I didn\u2019t give the tactical stuff a fair shake. I\u2019ll go back and have a review of them today.<br /> <br /> Anyone see any outstanding \u201cI Win\u201d social stuff? I think it\u2019s hard to top Argent Songbird at Ess1 really. (Buying 5 successes is nuts y\u2019all)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:29:14-07:00","id":1304368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1304364#post1304364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I am going to be perfectly honest, I didn\u2019t give the tactical stuff a fair shake. I\u2019ll go back and have a review of them today.<br /> <br /> Anyone see any outstanding \u201cI Win\u201d social stuff? I think it\u2019s hard to top Argent Songbird at Ess1 really. (Buying 5 successes is nuts y\u2019all)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh totally fair! I just have a weird habit of finding where Sorcery sits in a charm set and figuring out what else I can do with it. Solar Occult is honestly a little underwhelming but you CAN get a pet god so that's fun.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Intelligence Warfare is super good, all you need is a battle group with notable Might. If you can justify Might 3 you're laughing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T20:08:03-07:00","id":1304561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1304355#post1304355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shout out to Silver Lion Supremacy if you're a smart-guy tactician rather than a smart-guy sorcerer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Some more detail: Silver Lion Supremacy gives you those sweet non-charm dice on a Strategic manuever roll and it keys off Might, not Size. So even a small force of significantly empowered Followers will make a big difference. Assuming you describe your gambit, those babies are Successes.<br /> <br /> Combine with Raiton Follows After for its whopping 1m cost and you're getting extra non-charm dice from every 10 you roll, and the prereq Argent Pack Formation will basically end any penalties you might be concerned about.<br /> <br /> Another quick note, all of these key off the Might of any Allied battle group. Which means if there are NPC DBs on your side you don't even need the Followers merit.<br /> <br /> But you should have it, because this charm just turned you into Lunar Soren and you need some Laguz buddies.<br /> <br /> EDIT EDIT: Oh and if you're attacking a crashed opponent with RFA bc you're nasty like that you get basically a free full INT excellency as non-charm dice. Basically if you want to End someone's shit and you have even like, four magical friends, it's not out of the question that you could be rolling more Non-charm bonuses than your capped excellency is giving you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a good combo! (So good in fact, I recall Vance saying they'll be making a balance pass on it before the actual publication).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T20:12:33-07:00","id":1304563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1304364#post1304364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I am going to be perfectly honest, I didn\u2019t give the tactical stuff a fair shake. I\u2019ll go back and have a review of them today.<br /> <br /> Anyone see any outstanding \u201cI Win\u201d social stuff? I think it\u2019s hard to top Argent Songbird at Ess1 really. (Buying 5 successes is nuts y\u2019all)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Repurchasing Sense-Borrowing Method at E2 lets you use it on humans and it's pretty powerful as a scouting charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T22:54:45-07:00","id":1304577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1303671-prototype00\u2019s-lunar-ess2-charm-picks-with-no-ess2-pre-reqs-glory-sphere?p=1304561#post1304561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats a good combo! (So good in fact, I recall Vance saying they'll be making a balance pass on it before the actual publication).</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw maaaan. I should say I actually was mistaken, RFA is for orders, not manuevers. SLS still amazing as heck though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}